    "observed_behavior": "Angle.to_string carries seconds into the next minute half a unit too early at the rounding boundary, and with fields=1 it rounds seconds into minutes before rounding minutes into degrees (double rounding). Examples: Angle(\"1d2m59.49999s\").to_string(precision=0) gives \"1d03m00s\"; Angle(\"285d29m41.76s\").to_string(fields=1) gives \"286d\".",
    "expected_behavior": "Angle(\"1d2m59.49999s\").to_string(precision=0) should give \"1d02m59s\"; Angle(\"285d29m41.76s\").to_string(fields=1) should give \"285d\".",
    "manifestation": "wrong_value",
    "trigger_conditions": [
      "precision=0 with seconds just below the carry threshold (e.g. 59.49999s) so seconds should not round up to 60",
      "fields=1 with minutes/seconds such that seconds rounding into minutes would push degrees up (e.g. 285d29m41.76s)"
    ],
    "input_output_examples": [
